Vehicle: ModalAI Starling 2 Max, PX4 running on the VOXL 2 sensors DSP

##############################################################################
#  OUTDOOR PROFILE -- NOT PART OF THE COMMITTED 15-WEEK INTERNSHIP SCOPE
#  (8 Sep - 20 Dec 2026). The committed scope is indoor, netted-mocap-volume
#  flight only (see config/px4_starling_indoor.params and docs/SAFETY.md).
#
#  This file is provided as a forward-looking reference for a possible
#  post-internship outdoor phase. DO NOT LOAD THIS ONTO A VEHICLE without
#  ALL of the following in place:
#    - A licensed remote pilot in command for the flight (this project's
#      regulatory permits assume licensed-pilot supervision; that pilot
#      must physically be the one accepting outdoor risk, not the intern).
#    - A briefed, surveyed site: measured usable radius/height, obstacles,
#      wind limits, people/property nearby, and a written go/no-go brief
#      the pilot has signed off on for that specific site and day.
#    - Values below marked "MEASURE/CONFIRM" actually re-derived for that
#      site -- they are illustrative, not a substitute for a site survey.
##############################################################################

Flight context this file is tuned for:
  - Open outdoor site, line-of-sight RC and telemetry, no netting.
  - Same autonomy stack as indoor (Offboard mode, voxl-mapper trajectories
    via voxl-vision-hub offboard_mode="trajectory"), but with more space to
    both maneuver and to fail safely.
  - A licensed safety pilot holds a live RC link at all times, per
    docs/SAFETY.md.

File format: identical to config/px4_starling_indoor.params -- see that
file's header for the full column/type legend and the shared
research-verified facts (PX4 severity ordering, CP behaviour, reactive
geofence, etc.) that both profiles are built around. Only the deltas and
outdoor-specific rationale are repeated below.

# Vehicle-Id, Component-Id, Name, Value, Type
0	1	1	GF_MAX_HOR_DIST	50.000000	9
1	1	1	GF_MAX_VER_DIST	30.000000	9
2	1	1	GF_ACTION	3	6
3	1	1	COM_OF_LOSS_T	1.000000	9
4	1	1	COM_OBL_RC_ACT	0	6
5	1	1	COM_RC_LOSS_T	0.500000	9
6	1	1	NAV_RCL_ACT	2	6
7	1	1	COM_RCL_EXCEPT	0	6
8	1	1	CP_DIST	3.000000	9
9	1	1	CP_DELAY	0.400000	9
10	1	1	CP_GUIDE_ANG	30.000000	9
11	1	1	CP_GO_NO_DATA	0	6
12	1	1	MPC_POS_MODE	4	6
13	1	1	MPC_XY_VEL_MAX	5.000000	9
14	1	1	MPC_Z_VEL_MAX_UP	2.000000	9
15	1	1	MPC_Z_VEL_MAX_DN	1.500000	9
16	1	1	MPC_TILTMAX_AIR	35.000000	9
17	1	1	COM_OBS_AVOID	1	6

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-parameter rationale (deltas from the indoor profile, and why)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# GF_MAX_HOR_DIST = 50.0 m (float)  -- MEASURE/CONFIRM against the site
#   Illustrative radius for a modest open field. PX4's geofence is still
#   REACTIVE (it fires only after the boundary is crossed), so this must
#   be set with real margin inside whatever hard boundary the site brief
#   defines (property line, other airspace users, spectators), not set to
#   the boundary itself.
#
# GF_MAX_VER_DIST = 30.0 m (float)  -- MEASURE/CONFIRM against the
#   permit/site brief's altitude ceiling; set with margin below it for the
#   same reactive-geofence reason as above.
#
# GF_ACTION = 3 (Return) [int32]
#   Unlike indoor (Hold), Return is viable here because there is room to
#   fly a return path without it crossing close to people, obstacles, or
#   a net. PX4's own guidance is still that a STRICT boundary should use
#   Hold -- if the surveyed site is tight (proximity to a fence line,
#   spectators, or other restricted airspace), override this back to 2
#   (Hold) for that site's brief. Do not assume Return is always correct;
#   re-decide it per site.
#
# COM_OF_LOSS_T = 1.0 s (float)
#   Slightly longer than indoor's 0.5 s: outdoors, transient telemetry
#   dropouts (link range, terrain multipath) are more likely and less
#   immediately dangerous than indoors next to a person, so a little more
#   tolerance before declaring offboard lost is reasonable.
#
# COM_OBL_RC_ACT = 0 (Position) [int32]
#   Same reasoning as indoor: falls back to Position mode (not Land/RTL)
#   so the licensed pilot regains ordinary manual control immediately.
#   This is also what re-arms Collision Prevention per fact (1).
#
# COM_RC_LOSS_T = 0.5 s (float)
#   PX4 default; kept the same as indoor. No outdoor-specific reason to
#   relax an RC-loss detection timeout.
#
# NAV_RCL_ACT = 2 (Return) [int32]
#   Outdoors, with room to fly a return path, Return-to-launch is the
#   standard and generally safer choice on RC loss (get the vehicle back
#   to a known, cleared point) versus landing wherever it happens to be.
#   If the site brief identifies terrain/obstacles along the likely return
#   path, override to Land (3) for that site instead.
#
# COM_RCL_EXCEPT = 0 (no exceptions) [int32]
#   Unchanged from indoor; no mission phase in this project's scope
#   should suppress the RC-loss failsafe.
#
# CP_DIST = 3.0 m (float)
#   Larger than indoor's 1.0 m simply because there is more open space to
#   keep as standoff. Still only active in Position mode per fact (1) --
#   this is the piloted-testing safety net, not the autonomy layer's
#   avoidance.
#
# CP_DELAY, CP_GUIDE_ANG = unchanged (PX4 defaults, see indoor file for
#   rationale -- no outdoor-specific reason to move either).
#
# CP_GO_NO_DATA = 0 (disabled) [int32]
#   Kept conservative even outdoors: per fact (4), 0 means CP commands
#   zero velocity into any direction lacking sensor data (0.5 s watchdog,
#   5 s forces HOLD). With a person still being followed at close range
#   outdoors, "no data = don't move that way" remains the right default.
#
# MPC_POS_MODE = 4 (Smooth Position Control, acceleration-based) [int32]
#   Unchanged from indoor -- required for Collision Prevention to be
#   active at all per fact (1).
#
# MPC_XY_VEL_MAX = 5.0 m/s (float)  -- MEASURE/CONFIRM
#   Illustrative outdoor cap, well above the indoor 1.0 m/s. Must be
#   checked against the specific permit's speed limit (if any) and the
#   site's line-of-sight/reaction-distance budget for the safety pilot
#   before use.
#
# MPC_Z_VEL_MAX_UP / MPC_Z_VEL_MAX_DN = 2.0 / 1.5 m/s (float)
#   Scaled up from indoor in the same ratio, still keeping descent slower
#   than ascent.
#
# MPC_TILTMAX_AIR = 35 deg (float)
#   More permissive than indoor's 20 deg but still below the PX4 default
#   of ~45 deg, since the vehicle is still following a person at close
#   range even outdoors -- this is not an aerobatic/racing profile.
#
# COM_OBS_AVOID = 1 (enabled) [int32]
#   Unchanged from indoor -- see that file's note: this only lets
#   obstacle data through to PX4/telemetry, it does not itself make
#   avoidance active in Offboard mode. voxl-mapper routing around the
#   ESDF map remains the actual autonomous avoidance layer.
